ites of outstanding cultural significance were selected for excavation, including a late antique monastery in the north-east of the island and an Islamic town in the south-west. This paper provides an introduction to the Sīnīya Island Archaeological Project and presents the preliminary results of the excavations.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
